<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">South Persia Rifles</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1916">1916</a>–<a href="/years/1921">1921</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a> Rifles was a force of Iranian troops under British officers raised in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> in 1916, during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>, by Sir Percy Sykes. Intended to counter German agents and pro-German tribes, it fought the Qashqai under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ismail-khan-qashqai">Solat al-Dowleh</a> among others. The Iranian government never fully recognised it, and it was disbanded in 1921 as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reza-shah">Reza Khan</a> built a unified national army.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/south-persia-rifles.jpg" alt="South Persia Rifles" width="320" height="215" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Officers_and_men_of_the_South_Persia_Rifles,_c._1917.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
